{"title":"Brinewater Ports","sub":"Predictive maintenance: a $3.5M promise","type":"Investment / capacity","industry":"Ports and shipping","geo":"Singapore","diff":3,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"AI business case · bottleneck value · peak vs off-peak","prompt":"Brinewater runs a container terminal with 12 ship-to-shore cranes. A vendor offers AI that predicts crane breakdowns from sensor data, claiming it would cut unplanned downtime from 8% to 5% and add about $3.5M a year of container moves. It costs $1.2M to install and $0.4M a year to run. The terminal director asks for your view.","clarify":[{"q":"Crane operation?","a":"Each crane is available about 8,000 hours a year and moves about 30 containers an hour; each move earns about $40 of margin."},{"q":"Is the terminal full?","a":"For about four months a year (the peak season) ships queue and every crane hour is used. The rest of the year, cranes are often idle."},{"q":"Maintenance savings?","a":"Fewer emergency repairs and overtime would save about $0.6M a year."},{"q":"Other bottlenecks?","a":"None during peak; berths and yard have spare capacity."}],"structure":{"root":"Is predictive maintenance worth it for Brinewater?","branches":[{"head":"Extra crane hours","items":["Downtime reduction × hours"]},{"head":"Are those hours valuable?","items":["Only when cranes are the bottleneck"]},{"head":"Other savings","items":["Repairs, overtime, safety"]},{"head":"Costs","items":["Install","Running"]}]},"hypothesis":"Extra crane hours are only valuable when ships are waiting. Most of the year cranes are idle, so the vendor is probably overstating the value.","questions":[{"q":"Recreate the vendor's claim.","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Hours saved: 12 cranes × 8,000 × (8% − 5%) = 2,880. Containers: × 30 = 86,400; × $40 = <b>$3.46M</b> a year.</p>"},{"q":"Which of those hours actually add moves?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"388.459719pt\" hei