5 4736 Q 1408 4723 1421 4678 L 2842 1011 Q 2867 954 2892 957 Q 2918 960 2944 1018 L 4365 4666 Q 4390 4749 4461 4749 L 5107 4749 Q 5178 4749 5178 4666 L 5178 96 Q 5178 0 5082 0 L 4659 0 Q 4608 0 4585 19 Q 4563 38 4563 83 L 4563 3744 Q 4563 3776 4550 3773 Q 4538 3770 4531 3744 L 3123 83 Q 3091 0 3002 0 L 2694 0 Q 2592 0 2566 77 L 1178 3706 Q 1165 3738 1155 3734 Q 1146 3731 1146 3706 L 1146 83 Q 1146 38 1126 19 Q 1107 0 1056 0 L 710 0 L 710 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-dd\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-1f\" transform=\"translate(60.5 0)\"/></g></g></g><g id=\"patch_3\"><path d=\"M 51.025173 133.056 L 190.806991 133.056 L 190.806991 16.896 L 51.025173 16.896 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4868752c2e)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_4\"><path d=\"M 225.752446 133.056 L 365.534264 133.056 L 365.534264 90.210098 L 225.752446 90.210098 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4868752c2e)\" style=\"fill: #c2410c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_5\"><path d=\"M 35.299719 133.056 L 35.299719 11.088 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 35.299719 133.056 L 381.259719 133.056 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_8\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(115.119832 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" d=\"M 992 102 Q 992 0 877 0 L 429 0 Q 333 0 333 90 L 333 640 Q 333 723 403 723 L 928 723 Q 992 723 992 646 L 992 102 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" d=\"M 3456 4749 Q 3507 4749 3532 4723 Q 3558 4698 3552 4672 L 3546 4442 Q 3546 4390 3520 4329 Q 3494 4269 3456 4211 Q 3200 3827 2960 3385 Q 2720 2944 2515 2477 Q 2310 2010 2147 1571 Q 1984 1133 1875 758 Q 1766 384 1728 122 Q 1715 0 1632 0 L 1126 0 Q 1024 0 1050 109 Q 1139 467 1289 918 Q 1440 1370 1661 1891 Q 1882 2413 2182 2982 Q 2483 3552 2861 4147 Q 2886 4186 2880 4211 Q 2874 4237 2816 4237 L 339 4237 Q 262 4237 262 4314 L 307 4685 Q 314 4749 403 4749 L 3456 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-83\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(64.09375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" transform=\"translate(85 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_9\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(290.350855 88.242098) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" d=\"M 2470 4678 Q 2502 4717 2534 4733 Q 2566 4749 2630 4749 L 3059 4749 Q 3136 4749 3136 4672 L 3136 1792 Q 3136 1734 3187 1734 L 3789 1734 Q 3878 1734 3878 1670 L 3878 1357 Q 3878 1274 3789 1274 L 3194 1274 Q 3136 1274 3136 1210 L 3136 96 Q 3136 0 3034 0 L 2598 0 Q 2515 0 2515 83 L 2515 1229 Q 2515 1274 2458 1274 L 384 1274 Q 288 1274 288 1357 L 288 1683 Q 288 1728 313 1776 Q 339 1824 390 1894 L 2470 4678 L 2470 4678 z\nM 2445 1734 Q 2502 1734 2502 1779 L 2502 3910 Q 2502 3987 2483 3993 Q 2464 4000 2413 3936 L 851 1818 Q 787 1734 896 1734 L 2445 1734 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(67.40625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p4868752c2e\"><rect x=\"35.299719\" y=\"11.088\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Net yearly benefit, including maintenance savings and running costs ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Only during peak season, when ships are queuing: one-third of the year. Off-peak, a crane that would have broken down is simply replaced by an idle one.</p> <p>Valuable hours: 2,880 × 1/3 = 960; × 30 × $40 = <b>$1.15M</b>. Plus maintenance savings $0.6M, less $0.4M running: <b>$1.35M a year</b>.</p> <p>Payback on $1.2M: <b>0.9 years</b>. Still a good investment, but the extra moves are worth only a third of what the vendor claims ($1.15M vs $3.46M). On the same net basis as ours (adding maintenance savings, less running costs), the vendor's case would be $3.7M.</p>"},{"q":"How could Brinewater get more value from it?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Plan maintenance for the quiet months</b>, using the predictions to do repairs off-peak so cranes are fully available in peak season</li> <li>Negotiate the vendor's fee as a share of peak-season availability gains</li><li>Extend later to yard equipment if that becomes a bottleneck</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Invest, but expect about $1.4M of net yearly benefit, not the $3.7M the vendor's figures imply. Extra crane hours only add moves in the four-month peak, when ships queue; for the rest of the year cranes have spare time. Including $0.6M of maintenance savings, the system pays back in about 0.9 years. Use the predictions to shift maintenance into quiet months, and tie part of the vendor's fee to peak-season availability. Risk: sensor data quality on older cranes. Next step: pilot on the four busiest cranes.","great":["Rebuilds the vendor's figure","Values capacity only where it is the bottleneck","Includes maintenance savings and running costs","Finds a way to raise the value (shift maintenance off-peak)"],"id":78,"slug":"brinewater-ports"}